a quick way to scan a machine is with:
sudo nmap -sS -T4 --open --top-ports 20 (ip)

for scan TCP and UDP (but this scan ALL the open ports)
sudo nmap -sS -sU -p- <target>. 

you can select a limit by adding a number like this:
-sudo nmap -sS --top-ports 1000 <target>
sudo nmap -sS -p- --min-rate 5000 <target>

there are ways to scan ips or router by a sniky way 

-sS # 

- sudo nmap -sS -T2 192.168.1.5
- sudo nmap -sS -p22,80,443 192.168.1.1
